From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:37:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(miniwin): wait for one VBlank a frame on Citro3D

Flip waited for a VBlank after C3D_FrameEnd, and the next frame's
C3D_FrameBegin(C3D_FRAME_SYNCDRAW) waited for another, so every frame
gave up to one more refresh to waiting. Flip now waits only when the
frame drew nothing, which C3D_FrameBegin does not pace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/citro3d/renderer.cpp b/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/citro3d/renderer.cpp
index 8ee9e55..bd7a36e 100644
--- a/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/citro3d/renderer.cpp
+++ b/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/citro3d/renderer.cpp
@@ -738,10 +738,19 @@ void Citro3DRenderer::Flip()
 		g_rendering = false;
 		return;
 	}
+	if (!g_rendering) {
+		// Nothing drawn: no frame to end, and C3D_FrameBegin will not pace
+		// this one, so wait for the screen here.
+		gfxFlushBuffers();
+		gspWaitForVBlank();
+		return;
+	}
 	FlushImmediateVertices();
 	C3D_FrameEnd(0);
+	// C3D_FrameBegin(C3D_FRAME_SYNCDRAW) waits for the next VBlank before
+	// the next frame, so a second wait here would cost up to a refresh a
+	// frame. The flush keeps the top screen's console current.
 	gfxFlushBuffers();
-	gspWaitForVBlank();
 	g_rendering = false;
 }
 
